================================================================================================================================
RE-SCORED after the quote-mark and bold-Verdict fixes — 2026-08-27
================================================================================================================================
Two instrument bugs were found by hand-reading the raw replies above. NEITHER touches the
detection scorer, and the pre-registered thresholds are unchanged.

  1. `prompts.normalise_quote` stripped only the OUTER quotation marks, so a challenger
     quoting a judgment that itself quotes something — `Judgment says: "The sentence
     states: 'X'"` — had an accurate quotation recorded as a fabrication. Every quotation
     mark and markdown emphasis character now comes off BOTH sides. Every defect ever
     alleged was re-checked from the fixture text, with no calls: misattributed quotes
     fall from 30/155 to 8/154 (flash), 20/66 to 0/66 (gpt-4.1), 28/77 to 10/77 (mini),
     31/50 to 21/50 (nano), 10/95 to 8/95 (luna), 150/295 to 65/295 (qwen).
  2. `pick_auditor._VERDICT_LINE` did not match a bold `**Verdict: SOUND**`, so on 17 of
     the 59 contradiction items the appended sentence landed AFTER the decision line
     rather than before it. The regex now accepts markdown emphasis, the fixture was
     rebuilt, and exactly 19 variants changed — those 17, plus 2 misquotes that the
     quote-mark fix made injectable at a different quotation. Those 19 items (plus 1
     newly injectable misquote) were re-audited for all six candidates: 120 audits,
     $0.31. The rows they replace are kept in `rows-audit-<model>.superseded.jsonl`.
     15 controls whose surviving-defect set changed were graded again ($0.12).

Everything else on this page stands as measured. The table above is what the run
produced; the table below is the same measurements re-scored.

